# NEW (not in either report, found while triaging hunt-standard #1 and #13).
#
# `whichkey.leader` binds a BARE `ctrl+k` in the standard profile
# (src/commands/specs.zig, `.standard = &.{"ctrl+k"}`). Pressing it opens the
# which-key overlay, whose handler consumes the next key. Eighteen standard
# chords are spelled `ctrl+k <key>` — view.fullscreen, lsp.hover, git.commit,
# keys.edit, theme.toggle, the four focus-split chords and ten more — so none
# of them can ever fire in the profile that declares them.
#
# `Ctrl+K Ctrl+I` for lsp.hover is actively advertised in the Info panel.
#
# This asserts the advertised chord reaches its command. It fails on main:
# the leader popup opens instead and eats the tail.
write a.txt "alpha\n"
open a.txt
key ctrl+k
key z
# the leader overlay must NOT have taken the chord
expect screen lacks "no leader mapping"
expect screen lacks "<leader>"
